  "title": "Ebola Outbreak in DR Congo and Vaccine Doses",
  "summary": "The Democratic Republic of the Congo's Ebola outbreak continues to spread as 16,000 vaccine doses arrive, with health authorities warning of the virus's rapid spread and the risk of new cases. The doses are the first of 70,000 allocated to Kinshasa to address the crisis.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "DRC's Ebola outbreak has spread to a sixth province, with officials stating the disease is on track to become the deadliest in history.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over 2,100 people have been killed in the outbreak, compared to the 2014-16 outbreak's record of 755 cases.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "16,000 doses of Ervebo vaccine have been allocated to Kinshasa, with experts warning of the virus's exponential spread.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
